msgid "Tricount connection"
msgstr "Tricount connection"

msgid "Tricount connection info"
msgstr "This app connects to Tricount as an anonymous device — no email or password involved. When you register, a unique device identity (UUID + key pair) is created automatically. Tricount recognises you through that identity."

msgid "Register local account note"
msgstr "Your username and password are only for this web UI — they are not linked to tricount.com. On registration, an anonymous device identity is created automatically that the app uses to connect to Tricount."

msgid "Device credentials"
msgstr "Device credentials"

msgid "Device credentials info"
msgstr "This file contains the anonymous device identity this app uses to connect to Tricount. It is compatible with the Python tricount-api package (tricount_credentials.json). If you lose it, generate new credentials and re-join your tricounts using their sharing tokens. Note: a sharing token grants full read and write access — treat it like a password."

msgid "Password storage info"
msgstr "Your password is never stored in plain text. It is hashed with bcrypt (with a unique salt per password) before being saved to the database."

msgid "Tricount API credit"
msgstr "Tricount connectivity is powered by <a href=\"https://github.com/elrandar/tricount-api\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"underline hover:text-gray-600\">elrandar/tricount-api</a>."

